 r←Test_Misc_029(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;globalConfig;ns;parms;qdmx;success
⍝ Exercise `CheckForGit` the way `OpenProject` calls it when `batch` is 0, reporting the Git status.
⍝ APLGit2 1.0 changed the result of `Status` to a matrix, and `CheckForGit` crashed on it.
⍝ No other test noticed because they all open projects with batch←1, which skips `CheckForGit`.
⍝ The Git status of the Cider project is printed to the session.
⍝ *** Note that this function temporarily replaces Cider's global config file!
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 r←T._Failed

 :If ~##.Cider.G.IsGitInstalled
     r←T._NotApplicable ⋄ →0
 :EndIf

 globalConfig←##.Cider.GetCiderGlobalConfigFilename
 'Left-over from earlier test case?! Needs to be resolved!'Assert 0=⎕NEXISTS globalConfig,'.bkp'
 (globalConfig,'.bkp')⎕NMOVE globalConfig   ⍝ Save Cider's original global config file
 ns←⎕NS''
 ns.ReportGitStatus←2                      ⍝ Report in the session: 1 would open ⎕ED, 3 would ask
 ∆SaveCiderGlobalConfig ns
 parms←⎕NS''
 parms.batch←0
 qdmx←⍬
 :Trap 0
     success←##.Cider.CheckForGit ##.CiderConfig.HOME(⎕NS'')parms
 :Else
     qdmx←⎕DMX
 :EndTrap
 ⎕NDELETE globalConfig
 globalConfig ⎕NMOVE globalConfig,'.bkp'   ⍝ Restore the original before checking anything

 →T.GoToTidyUp ⍬≢qdmx
 →T.GoToTidyUp 1≢success

 r←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
⍝Done
